{"text": "The very fact that all of our experiences take place in a physical space makes the space inseparable from what defines it, from the event that took place in it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The tree and the ground beneath are inseparable from what took place there. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This intertwining of space, place, and experience challenges the idea of place as passive backdrop. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If place and space are central to the very heart of experience, we must accept the possibility that the spatial framework is the medium of all experiences, actions, thoughts, memories, and feelings of every place, not merely a background or context exterior to experience as commonly supposed. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Belgian literary critic Georges Poulet made the point elegantly, writing of the space created in Marcel Prousts great novel In Search of Lost Time, Beings surround themselves with the places where they find themselves, the way one wraps oneself up in a garment that is at one and the same time a disguise and a characterization. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Without places, beings would be only abstractions.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "f", "a", "c", "t", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "a", "l", "l", " ", "o", "f", " ", "o", "u", "r", " ", "e", "x", "p", "e", "r", "i", "e", "n", "c", "e", "s", " ", "t", "a", "k", "e", " ", "p", "l", "a", "c", "e", " ", "i", "n", " ", "a", " ", "p", "h", "y", "s", "i", "c", "a", "l", " ", "s", "p", "a", "c", "e", " ", "m", "a", "k", "e", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "p", "a", "c", "e", " ", "i", "n", "s", "e", "p", "a", "r", "a", "b", "l", "e", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "w", "h", "a", "t", " ", "d", "e", "f", "i", "n", "e", "s", " ", "i", "t", ",", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "e", "v", "e", "n", "t", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "t", "o", "o", "k", " ", "p", "l", "a", "c", "e", " ", "i", "n", " ", "i", "t", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a"